# MatrixMedia self-host — non-secret configuration.
#
# install.sh writes a real .env for you from its CLI flags; this file documents
# every knob and its default. Secrets are NOT here — they are generated once into
# .env.secrets by lib/secrets.sh and never rotate. Never commit a populated .env
# or .env.secrets.
#
# First-start seeds: a knob marked "first-start seed" below feeds a setting that
# Operator Console → System → Settings owns. mm-core copies its value into the
# database at its first start (a secret at the first start where it is non-empty and
# MM_SETTINGS_ENCRYPTION_KEY is set, which install.sh generates) and ignores the .env
# value from then on: change it in the dashboard instead. The .env value is used
# again only as the break-glass fallback, with MM_SETTINGS_SAFE_MODE=1.
# See deploy/docs/settings.md. Every other knob here stays .env-managed.

# --- required ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Apex domain you own. Synapse server_name + all routing derive from this.
# Federation/well-known is served at the apex; services live at matrix.${MM_DOMAIN}.
MM_DOMAIN=example.com

# Public IPv4 of this host (coturn external-ip, livekit node_ip, mm-switch).
# install.sh auto-detects this in preflight; override only if detection is wrong.
MM_PUBLIC_IP=203.0.113.10

# Email for Let's Encrypt registration / expiry notices.
ACME_EMAIL=you@example.com

# --- images -----------------------------------------------------------------
# DO NOT SET THESE. The image set is pinned in versions.env, which compose reads BEFORE
# .env — so anything you put here OVERRIDES the pins and un-pins the stack.
#
# This file used to ship MM_REGISTRY=ghcr.io/matrixmedia (an org that does not exist) and a
# stale MM_VERSION. Since `mmctl init` and the README both tell you to write your .env from
# this file, anyone following the documented path got a stack that 404s at pull time.
#
# Only set one of these if you deliberately want to deviate from the shipped, tested set —
# e.g. to pin your own build:
#   MM_REGISTRY=ghcr.io/your-org
#   MM_VERSION=1.2.3

# --- TLS --------------------------------------------------------------------
# MM_TLS_MODE: set automatically by install.sh. http01 is the only supported mode until the P2 vendor-DNS work lands.
MM_TLS_MODE=http01

# --- message retention ------------------------------------------------------
# OFF by default: Synapse keeps history forever and deletes nothing.
#
# Turning this on makes Synapse PERMANENTLY DELETE message history older than
# MM_RETENTION_MAX_LIFETIME, on a purge job that runs every 12h. It is irreversible —
# events are removed, not tombstoned. Only enable it if you have actually decided you want
# it (storage cost, a privacy policy, a legal obligation).
#
# MM_RETENTION_MAX_LIFETIME is ignored while MM_RETENTION_ENABLED=false; it exists so the
# value you would get is visible before you flip the switch.
MM_RETENTION_ENABLED=false
MM_RETENTION_MIN_LIFETIME=1d
MM_RETENTION_MAX_LIFETIME=90d

# --- payments ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Demo mode wires the in-stack mm-fakestripe + mock Lightning so the full
# monetization UI works with NO real money. NEVER set true on a real-money host.
# MM_DEMO_MODE is a first-start seed for mm-core's Demo mode setting (Settings →
# Monetization). It also selects the compose demo profile (mm-fakestripe, LNbits)
# on every start, which stays .env-managed, as does MM_ALLOW_MOCK.
MM_DEMO_MODE=false
MM_ALLOW_MOCK=false

# MM_TEMP_MODE: true only for --no-domain throwaway installs (sslip.io, self-signed TLS, no federation).
MM_TEMP_MODE=false

# Stripe API base. Demo points at the fakestripe sidecar; real money uses Stripe.
# Read-only in the dashboard: it stays .env-managed.
MM_STRIPE_API_BASE=https://api.stripe.com/

# Real Stripe credentials (leave blank in demo mode). Both are first-start seeds: after
# mm-core has stored them, rotate or go live in Settings → Monetization (Replace, Save,
# Apply & restart); a new value here is ignored.
MM_STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
MM_STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# --- optional: "Request Server" notifications --------------------------------
# When a dashboard user submits a Request Server form, the request is stored and
# (if this is set) a notification is POSTed here (Slack-compatible {"text": ...}).
# This is a first-start seed: after mm-core has stored it, change it in Settings →
# General.
MM_SERVER_REQUEST_WEBHOOK_URL=

# --- optional: more first-start seeds ----------------------------------------
# The compose template passes these to mm-core with the defaults shown. Setting one
# here only matters before mm-core's first start; afterwards change it in Settings.
# LNbits keys are empty (not configured) unless set.
# MM_MONETIZATION_ENABLED=true
# MM_MONETIZATION_DONATIONS_ENABLED=true
# MM_MONETIZATION_SUBSCRIPTIONS_ENABLED=true
# MM_ADVERTISING_ENABLED=true
# MM_FEDERATION_ENABLED=true
# MM_LNBITS_ENABLED=false
# MM_LNBITS_INVOICE_KEY=
# MM_LNBITS_ADMIN_KEY=
# MM_TURN_TTL_SECS=86400
